   <span style="font-size: 10.0pt;">Differences in timing of revenue recognition, billings, and cash collections result in receivables.&#160;&#160;Generally, billing occurs subsequent to revenue recognition, resulting in unbilled revenue on the balance sheet.&#160;&#160;The Company does not receive advances or deposits from customers before revenue is recognized so no contract liabilities are reported.&#160;&#160;Accounts receivable are recorded when the right to consideration becomes unconditional and are presented separately on the balance sheet.&#160;&#160;The changes in accounts receivable &#8211; customers and in unbilled revenue were primarily due to the normal timing difference between performance and the customer&#8217;s payments.</span>
